    "text": "In the Ciphera repository, `glyph` means raw sensor inputs, and `sigil` means processed classifications. `NodeGate` reads `glyph` from `/var/ciphera/in/node.glf` through `data.input_path` and writes `sigil` to `/var/ciphera/out/node.sig` through `data.output_path`. For input specifications, see the [glyph spec](https://doc.ciphera.invalid/glyph) and select **Raw Glyph**. For output specifications, see the [sigil spec](https://doc.ciphera.invalid/sigil) and select **Processed Sigil**. Preserve the error `ERR_GLYPH expected glyph got sigil`.",
